1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:05,006
The solution to case PORTFLOW, and everything to check before you submit.

2
00:00:06,010 --> 00:00:15,439
Our answer: option B, Dynamic yard: demand zoning, MIP/CRAFT slotting, tracking database, AI AGV pilot.

3
00:00:15,439 --> 00:00:26,242
It delivers 21.7 percent against a target of 19.5 percent, for 9.40 million dollars of a 10.00 million dollars budget.

4
00:00:27,240 --> 00:00:29,007
Option B is recommended.

5
00:00:29,007 --> 00:00:34,824
It is both the cheapest compliant option and the best value: a dominant choice.

6
00:00:35,820 --> 00:00:47,047
The package has 7 initiatives for 9.40 million dollars upfront, 1.30 million dollars a year to run, and 6.40 million dollars a year of savings.

7
00:00:47,047 --> 00:00:55,212
Using the case formula, the five-year net financial impact is minus 16.10 million dollars, a net saving.

8
00:00:56,210 --> 00:01:19,946
Operations & Safety: Zoning and slotting: fast movers near exits, stacks by pickup order Supply Chain: One database feeds lines, trucks, rail and customers Organizational Change Management: Co-design before tools; paid training; drivers can become AGV supervisors AI & Automation: MIP + CRAFT layout; weekly dynamic slotting; planners approve

9
00:01:20,950 --> 00:01:31,966
The economics: a run-rate benefit of 6.40 million dollars a year, net present value of 6.09 million dollars, and payback in 33 months.

10
00:01:32,970 --> 00:01:34,042
Now stress it.

11
00:01:34,042 --> 00:01:43,080
If performance falls fifteen percent and costs rise twenty, the gain is 18.45 percent and NPV is 140 thousand dollars.

12
00:01:43,080 --> 00:01:48,288
The target would be missed, which is why the pilot gate comes first.

13
00:01:48,288 --> 00:01:53,802
The most sensitive driver is annual benefit: achieved gain x unit value.

14
00:01:54,800 --> 00:01:57,686
Days 1 to 30: Validate & pilot.

15
00:01:57,686 --> 00:02:02,248
Confirm baseline data and the binding constraint.

16
00:02:02,248 --> 00:02:05,041
Days 31 to 60: Prove & decide.

17
00:02:05,041 --> 00:02:14,350
Pilot gate: Layout model beats today's travel by at least 20% in simulation; AGV safety case signed.

18
00:02:14,350 --> 00:02:17,236
Days 61 to 90: Scale & control.

19
00:02:17,236 --> 00:02:20,960
Begin re-zone, go dynamic, pilot 2 agvs.

20
00:02:21,960 --> 00:02:34,866
The three risks to manage: AGV breakdown or navigation fault, mitigated by preventive maintenance plan and vendor sla, sensor health monitoring, fenced lane, manual tractors as instant fallback.

21
00:02:34,866 --> 00:02:46,309
Tracking or database errors (wrong slot recorded), mitigated by ocr and crane-sensor double check on every move, nightly reconciliation audit, manual search procedure kept.

22
00:02:46,309 --> 00:02:52,296
AI slotting or demand forecast wrong, mitigated by re-slots run weekly on actual bookings.

23
00:02:53,300 --> 00:02:58,004
Question: Why not just build on the 15-acre parcel?

24
00:02:58,004 --> 00:03:08,149
Answer: Space alone fails the objective: 25,344 / 28,000 TEU = 90.5% at year 5, for about $14.5M, over budget.

25
00:03:08,149 --> 00:03:14,144
Cutting dwell to 4.7 days reaches about 83% on today's footprint.

26
00:03:14,144 --> 00:03:16,727
Question: Why only two AGVs?

27
00:03:16,727 --> 00:03:28,071
Answer: The evidence is mixed: successful automated terminals cut operating costs 25-55%, but some lose 7-15% productivity.

28
00:03:28,071 --> 00:03:39,692
Two units in a fenced lane prove uptime, cost per move and safety for $1.6M; the fleet grows only if the month-12 gate passes.

29
00:03:40,690 --> 00:03:43,445
Before you submit, run the checklist.

30
00:03:43,445 --> 00:03:45,306
10 of 11 items are ready.

31
00:03:45,306 --> 00:03:48,955
Still open: assumptions validated with real data.

32
00:03:48,955 --> 00:03:55,954
Replace the assumptions with real data if you can, or state them clearly on an appendix slide.

33
00:03:56,950 --> 00:04:02,276
Lead with the answer, prove it with three numbers, and own the risks.

34
00:04:02,276 --> 00:04:02,970
Option B.

35
00:04:02,970 --> 00:04:03,742
Good luck.
